sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, one Swamp run with the shared route reconcile child (route.reconcile). docs/reference/routes.md#change-a-tld-cluster-state-or-cluster-membership.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: cluster:update
  %% kind: cluster.update
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane V icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Cluster Nodes<br/>Router · members
  participant V as DNS targets<br/>resolvers · peers
  CLI->>GW: cluster:update<br/>CLUSTER options
  Note over GW: Validate, lock, plan<br/>transitions stored
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has an access grant to a member Node, or to the Gateway Node when the Cluster has none
  %%> - at least one of `--name` and `--tld` (`cluster.update_required`); the name and TLD are valid and free
  %%> - a new TLD on an active Cluster needs one active Router (`cluster.router_required`) and no non-member Node that owns it (`cluster.tld_conflict`), and keeps the private names within the DNS policy limit (`vpn.peer_dns_policy_invalid`)
  %%> - every affected Route keeps a valid domain, scope and target, and a generated Route keeps an effective TLD; one refusal leaves every Route in place; an active public Route that the change would move is refused (`route.reconciliation_required`)
  %%> - no other Cluster change runs; the Gateway waits up to 30 seconds, then refuses with `cluster.router_busy`
  %%> Stored:
  %%> - the Cluster keeps its name and TLD; a pending replacement is stored for each domain change and the old placement for each scope change
  alt active Cluster and the TLD changes, or an earlier change is unfinished
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-cluster-update
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    SW->>V: Add the new TLD in DNS<br/>child dns-publish
    %%> DNS lifecycle:
    %%> - the shared publication checks the VPN and Cluster projections, moves affected LAN member policies, and holds old resolver cleanup until every member confirms (ADR 0248)
    %%> Why first:
    %%> - the new names must resolve before the child withdraws the old sites; the old TLD keeps answering
    %%> Managed peers:
    %%> - affected LAN members receive the new domains inside this shared publication before cleanup; unrelated peers keep their normal reconcile path
    opt Routes change
      SW->>N: Reconcile the Routes<br/>child route-reconcile
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - moves every generated Route to the new TLD, or back to its Node TLD when the TLD is unset; the cutover is inside the child
    end
    SW->>V: Prune old DNS answers<br/>child dns-publish
    %%> DNS lifecycle:
    %%> - the shared publication checks the VPN and Cluster projections, moves affected LAN member policies, and holds old resolver cleanup until every member confirms (ADR 0248)
    %%> Why it always runs:
    %%> - it removes only what the stored state does not need, so after a failure before the cutover it removes the new TLD again
    alt every step succeeds
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      Note over GW: Record name and TLD<br/>Routes cut over
    else a step fails
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      Note over GW: Read the failed step<br/>cutover or not
      %%> Result before the cutover:
      %%> - the Cluster keeps its name and TLD and every Route keeps its domain and scope
      %%> Result after the cutover:
      %%> - the new name and TLD are in force; a rerun finishes the withdrawal and the prune
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - run the same command again; every step runs again and skips what already matches
    end
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
    end
  else name only, inactive Cluster, or no change, nothing unfinished
    GW-->>CLI: 200 OK<br/>Cluster updated
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the name and TLD are recorded at once; no Node is contacted and no traffic changes
    %%> Skipped:
    %%> - when the values already match and nothing is unfinished, the result reports `Skipped — nothing to change (cluster.update_unchanged)`
  end
